536
00:38:45,761 --> 00:38:47,430
Hey, Soo-hyun's on TV.

537
00:38:47,513 --> 00:38:51,183
Police have identified two suspects
and are tracking them.

538
00:38:51,267 --> 00:38:53,894
For more,
we go to our reporter at the scene.

539
00:38:53,978 --> 00:38:58,065
Yes, I'm at the Hangang River in Seoul,
where the body was found.

540
00:38:58,149 --> 00:39:03,070
A citizen reported a body floating
in the Hangang River this morning.

541
00:39:03,154 --> 00:39:06,031
The victim is the father
of the recently-abducted kindergartener

542
00:39:06,115 --> 00:39:07,366
who has since returned home.

543
00:39:07,450 --> 00:39:08,826
You fucking bastard.

544
00:39:08,909 --> 00:39:10,453
Why are you doing this?

545
00:39:10,536 --> 00:39:11,495
What now?

546
00:39:11,579 --> 00:39:13,247
The police are after you two.

547
00:39:13,330 --> 00:39:15,166
Just shut up and answer my question!

548
00:39:17,042 --> 00:39:19,044
Why the hell are you doing this?

549
00:39:21,797 --> 00:39:23,382
That's for you to find out.

550
00:39:24,091 --> 00:39:25,551
I'll be waiting. Hurry.

551
00:39:26,385 --> 00:39:27,845
I haven't got much time.

552
00:39:29,388 --> 00:39:30,431
See you again.

553
00:39:32,308 --> 00:39:35,686
They are looking into his ties
to the suspects.

554
00:39:35,769 --> 00:39:38,230
The investigation is in its early stages,

555
00:39:38,314 --> 00:39:40,733
and all possibilities
are being considered.

556
00:39:40,816 --> 00:39:45,863
Police also urged the media
to avoid unverified rumors

557
00:39:45,946 --> 00:39:48,616
and sensational coverage of the case.

558
00:39:48,699 --> 00:39:51,368
That fucking dumbass.

559
00:39:56,707 --> 00:39:58,042
Hey, we need to run.

560
00:39:58,542 --> 00:40:01,795
It's probably hacked.
Memorize the number and ditch it.

561
00:40:02,755 --> 00:40:05,007
Grab your clothes. For fuck's sake.

562
00:40:07,510 --> 00:40:10,596
TWO SUSPECTS IDENTIFIED AND BEING TRACKED

563
00:40:34,328 --> 00:40:35,621
Soo-hyun!

564
00:40:36,247 --> 00:40:37,081
Damn it!

565
00:40:37,164 --> 00:40:38,874
Soo-hyun, talk to me!

566
00:40:39,375 --> 00:40:40,251
Soo-hyun!

567
00:40:52,304 --> 00:40:54,265
They say it shows signs of suicide.

568
00:40:56,809 --> 00:41:00,354
His daughter was kidnapped.
You think suicide makes sense?

569
00:41:00,437 --> 00:41:01,272
It doesn't.

570
00:41:03,315 --> 00:41:05,067
"Was not a suicide."

571
00:41:05,150 --> 00:41:06,944
That's what the tip said as well.

572
00:41:08,445 --> 00:41:10,698
And he was the landlord,

573
00:41:11,198 --> 00:41:13,492
and the bastard living there
is the kidnapper.

574
00:41:15,244 --> 00:41:18,706
Fuck. Where do I even start?

575
00:41:23,586 --> 00:41:24,420
I don't know.

576
00:41:26,171 --> 00:41:28,007
You were taken to Noja's agency,

577
00:41:28,090 --> 00:41:30,259
then dragged out by two thugs.

578
00:41:30,342 --> 00:41:32,678
Your address was on Noja's computer.

579
00:41:33,304 --> 00:41:34,513
I don't know anything.

580
00:41:42,146 --> 00:41:43,981
I'm not here to bust you for gambling.

581
00:41:44,064 --> 00:41:47,860
I'm not interested in you.
I just need to get this bastard. Hey.

582
00:41:48,360 --> 00:41:49,570
Hey.

583
00:41:50,279 --> 00:41:53,407
I'll fucking get them for you.
Just tell me if you know this bastard.

584
00:41:55,200 --> 00:41:56,702
Even if I did, I can't say.

585
00:41:58,454 --> 00:42:01,040
I could end up
as fucking unclaimed remains.

586
00:42:09,673 --> 00:42:12,217
Those bastards are all in it together.

587
00:42:12,301 --> 00:42:15,387
They lend you money for gambling.
If you run, they come get you.

588
00:42:15,471 --> 00:42:18,057
It's either your identity or your organs.
Detective.

589
00:42:20,267 --> 00:42:21,852
Detective, what would you sell?

590
00:42:22,895 --> 00:42:25,814
They steal identities
from the homeless and those in debt.

591
00:42:25,898 --> 00:42:28,567
If things go south,
they kill them and stage it as a suicide.

592
00:42:28,651 --> 00:42:31,362
So don't ever come looking for me.

593
00:42:31,445 --> 00:42:33,155
I've got nothing left but my life.

594
00:42:34,531 --> 00:42:36,408
Hey.

595
00:43:00,641 --> 00:43:02,267
A man died.

596
00:43:02,893 --> 00:43:04,770
He just jumped off the bridge.

597
00:43:06,313 --> 00:43:09,650
Anyway, because of Noja,
cops will be everywhere.

598
00:43:10,567 --> 00:43:13,612
That bastard's not as sharp
as he used to be.

599
00:43:16,657 --> 00:43:18,158
It's not just his problem.

600
00:43:18,242 --> 00:43:20,911
The pigs were onto me,
so I had to move my operation.

601
00:43:20,994 --> 00:43:24,623
So you gotta help me out here.

602
00:43:24,707 --> 00:43:25,916
How?

603
00:43:28,544 --> 00:43:29,503
Noja.

604
00:43:29,586 --> 00:43:31,630
Gotta deal with him
before the cops get to us.

605
00:43:31,714 --> 00:43:34,717
I tried to talk to him,
but nothing fucking got through.

606
00:43:35,759 --> 00:43:37,678
Get some guys to take care of Noja.

607
00:43:37,761 --> 00:43:39,263
We need to bury both bastards.

608
00:43:40,180 --> 00:43:42,307
I've been living like this lately too.

609
00:43:42,391 --> 00:43:44,226
I don't really have anyone to call.

610
00:43:46,687 --> 00:43:47,938
That's your problem.

611
00:43:48,522 --> 00:43:50,524
Wanna keep your hands fucking clean, huh?

612
00:43:50,607 --> 00:43:54,194
We're in this together.
Don't act like it's not your problem.

613
00:43:54,278 --> 00:43:55,487
Fuck, I…

614
00:43:55,988 --> 00:43:59,408
I'm only asking nicely because it's you.

615
00:43:59,491 --> 00:44:01,368
Who gave you that identity?

616
00:44:01,452 --> 00:44:03,078
I did, didn't I?

617
00:44:03,162 --> 00:44:04,621
When you were on the run,

618
00:44:04,705 --> 00:44:07,166
everyone thought
you were fucking in the Philippines.

619
00:44:07,249 --> 00:44:09,710
Bullshit. You've never fucking been there.

620
00:44:12,129 --> 00:44:15,966
-I mean, I do appreciate that--
-What about this place?

621
00:44:16,049 --> 00:44:18,385
Who got you a job so you could get by?

622
00:44:19,178 --> 00:44:21,764
Is this fucking business yours?!

623
00:44:22,806 --> 00:44:26,602
Hey, you fucking bastard!
You're just the front! Act like one!

624
00:44:34,151 --> 00:44:35,068
Myeong-su.

625
00:44:36,403 --> 00:44:38,864
You're just here to take the hit for me.

626
00:44:41,867 --> 00:44:43,952
You're fucking nothing.

627
00:44:45,829 --> 00:44:49,541
Just say yes when I ask nicely.

628
00:44:52,252 --> 00:44:53,253
I'll try to find some.

629
00:44:58,008 --> 00:44:59,134
I'll find some.

630
00:45:06,183 --> 00:45:07,017
But you know,

631
00:45:07,100 --> 00:45:10,229
this has nothing to do with me, okay?

632
00:45:10,979 --> 00:45:11,980
I know.

633
00:45:22,741 --> 00:45:25,661
And run the site better.

634
00:45:25,744 --> 00:45:26,870
Boost the odds a bit.

635
00:45:26,954 --> 00:45:30,582
That's how you get
those little bastards swarming in.

636
00:45:30,666 --> 00:45:31,625
Okay?

637
00:45:33,001 --> 00:45:33,919
Okay.

638
00:45:36,505 --> 00:45:37,631
Hey, Mr. Kwak!

639
00:45:37,714 --> 00:45:39,091
Lend me some money.

640
00:45:39,842 --> 00:45:42,928
Damn, I'm running cold today.

641
00:45:44,805 --> 00:45:46,890
Sir. I'll head out now.

642
00:45:46,974 --> 00:45:48,141
Yeah, sure.

643
00:45:48,225 --> 00:45:49,268
Sir.

644
00:46:03,490 --> 00:46:06,159
The cards just aren't going my way.

645
00:46:06,243 --> 00:46:09,663
The flow keeps breaking,
and my timing's been off all day.

646
00:46:10,163 --> 00:46:14,209
It may not look like much,
but it's been fully serviced.

647
00:46:14,293 --> 00:46:15,878
It's a great car, Noja.

648
00:46:15,961 --> 00:46:17,254
What do you drive?

649
00:46:17,337 --> 00:46:18,964
Me? I drive…

650
00:46:20,382 --> 00:46:21,425
Over there.

651
00:46:22,509 --> 00:46:23,510
Nice.

652
00:46:24,636 --> 00:46:25,470
Swap with me.

653
00:46:26,388 --> 00:46:29,933
-Noja, the price of that car is--
-I'm heading out of town.

654
00:46:30,809 --> 00:46:31,810
-Huh?
-Keys.

655
00:46:33,061 --> 00:46:34,187
Noja.

656
00:46:34,688 --> 00:46:35,647
Come on, Noja!

657
00:46:35,731 --> 00:46:39,276
I finally went all out
and had the whole car reconditioned.

658
00:46:39,359 --> 00:46:41,111
Come on!

659
00:46:42,654 --> 00:46:43,530
Keys.

660
00:46:46,283 --> 00:46:47,534
Goddamn it.

661
00:46:48,702 --> 00:46:49,745
This is…

662
00:47:03,508 --> 00:47:05,552
No name on that rat bastard's number.

663
00:47:05,636 --> 00:47:07,054
It's a burner phone.

664
00:47:07,137 --> 00:47:08,931
This is a burner phone too. Use it.

665
00:47:09,014 --> 00:47:11,308
Don't call or text anyone.
Only use it with me.

666
00:47:14,519 --> 00:47:15,604
Hey, is that the one?

667
00:47:15,687 --> 00:47:17,648
Yeah, it is. How did you get it?

668
00:47:18,482 --> 00:47:21,568
You can get drugs delivered these days.
This is nothing.

669
00:47:22,152 --> 00:47:23,403
By the way,

670
00:47:24,529 --> 00:47:26,239
why do you wear fake glasses?

671
00:47:26,740 --> 00:47:28,450
I just feel more at ease.

672
00:47:28,533 --> 00:47:31,078
You're a weird little bastard, aren't you?

673
00:47:31,161 --> 00:47:33,747
What, is it like a mask?

674
00:47:35,415 --> 00:47:36,500
Why would I wear one?

675
00:47:37,125 --> 00:47:39,086
That's what guilty bastards do.

676
00:47:39,169 --> 00:47:41,922
They keep hiding things,
covering them up, and changing them.

677
00:47:43,924 --> 00:47:45,384
So, have you thought about it?

678
00:47:51,306 --> 00:47:53,392
I'm starving. Fuck, let's go eat.

679
00:48:18,208 --> 00:48:19,042
Moon-jae!

680
00:48:21,253 --> 00:48:22,170
Moon-jae!

681
00:48:23,839 --> 00:48:24,965
I think I know him.

682
00:48:29,344 --> 00:48:30,178
Who is he?

683
00:48:42,357 --> 00:48:43,608
Aren't you getting in?

684
00:48:56,621 --> 00:48:58,832
Spit it out, punk. Who the hell is he?

685
00:49:01,668 --> 00:49:03,962
I knew him at university.

686
00:49:04,046 --> 00:49:05,881
He was kinda like, you know…

687
00:49:06,673 --> 00:49:08,425
He really envied me.

688
00:49:09,718 --> 00:49:10,552
Jealous, I guess.

689
00:49:11,553 --> 00:49:12,846
Jealous?

690
00:49:12,929 --> 00:49:13,764
Not a grudge?

691
00:49:16,308 --> 00:49:17,309
No.

692
00:49:18,685 --> 00:49:19,936
It wasn't like that.

693
00:49:22,647 --> 00:49:26,109
If it's not a grudge,
why the fuck is he pulling this shit?

694
00:49:27,569 --> 00:49:28,737
No idea.

695
00:49:28,820 --> 00:49:30,989
But I can't shake the feeling it's him.

696
00:49:31,656 --> 00:49:33,825
Really? Then we should run with it.

697
00:49:42,542 --> 00:49:44,377
That'll be 228,000 won.

698
00:50:29,172 --> 00:50:30,841
Where do we go to get that bastard?

699
00:50:30,924 --> 00:50:31,842
An island.

700
00:50:33,260 --> 00:50:34,219
An island?

701
00:50:41,852 --> 00:50:43,103
Where?

702
00:50:47,649 --> 00:50:49,401
VINTORA STEAKHOUSE
118,000 WON APPROVED

703
00:50:53,446 --> 00:50:54,281
Hey.

704
00:50:56,783 --> 00:50:57,659
What the hell?

705
00:55:59,127 --> 00:56:02,046
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang

